'''''Cenchrus orientale''''', previously '''''Pennisetum orientale''''', commonly known as the '''oriental fountain grass''', is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the grass [[family (botany)|family]] Poaceae, [[native species|native]] to North West Asia and North Africa. Growing to {{convert|60 |cm|in|abbr=on}} tall and broad, this decorative perennial grass forms clumps with multiple tufted [[panicle]]s up to {{convert|14 |cm|in|abbr=on}} in length. The panicles are pale pink, maturing to brown.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.gardenia.net/plant/pennisetum-orientale-oriental-fountain-grass | title = Pennisetum orientale
| publisher = Gardenia.net | accessdate = 22 April 2018}}</ref>

The plant is not entirely hardy, disliking prolonged freezing temperatures. In cultivation it requires a sheltered position and some winter protection in colder areas. It has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref name = RHSPF>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/70387/i-Pennisetum-orientale-i/Details | title = RHS Plantfinder - ''Pennisetum orientale''
| accessdate = 23 April 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/agm-lists/agm-ornamentals.pdf | title = AGM Plants - Ornamental | date = July 2017 | page = 75 | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | accessdate = 22 April 2018}}</ref>

